Z||000000||fierospeeder||12-02-1999||02:26 AM||||I got addicted to Ebay also.  I saw two fiero magazines from road and track this one guy was selling and i got the magazines today in the mail.  The one is a road and track may 1981 issue and it shows the fiero being a prototype.  I dont have a scanner so im sorry but i will scan it when i get one.<BR>The title of the article is "pontiac P-Car"<BR>2000Lb 2 seat mid engine commuter car (reads sports car)<BR>GM is trying to gain some market to compete against fiat X1/9 and the mazda RX-7, also the triumph tr7.<BR>The code name of the car is the P-car.  "it will probably be called the sunfire"  and be introduced in the spring of 82.<BR>it is being sold as a communter car, and give racing a good rap.<BR>It will be priced under 8000 dollars.<BR>The engine will probably be a two throttle body injected TBI engine, possibility are 2.5L Iron duke and a Brazilian built 1.8L overhead camshaft 4 cylinder.  GM is listing the 1.8L as the base engine but the 2.5 will be probably available at the start of the production.  "Another possibility further down the road is a chevrolet-designed 60-degree v-6"  giving 180bhp.  If the v-6 falls, an alternative would be a turbocharged(maybe supercharged?) version of the iron duke.  They talk about how the cradle is a great idea because its away from the cabin, less noise and full independent suspension.  Better traction.  4,5speed and auto trans will be offered.  It talks about the design of the body, steel frame and plastic skins, SMC.  and later in date it will be made out of RRIM urethane.  "GM is hoping for 50 mpg at a steady 50mph."  "Production of the P-car will be in the region of 75,000 the first year, ultimately rising to 100,000."  This is a four page article showing pictures of the prototype in 81.  It shows three pictures with 2 different so called P-cars.  One is red which looks like my 84 SE  with no trunk lid, gay wheels, and no front hood.  A silver one with all its hoods, has a type of a corvette tail, and a GT kind of a look in front fascia.   Theres a 3D drawn picture of the car inside out, like haynes does,  instead of the spare being in front its in the back where our trunk space is, and the front looks like its the luggage compartment like the beetle,  which i own.<BR>So our fiero could have been called the sunfire how weird.<P>The other magazine i got was a road and track sept. 83, just an introduction to the fiero and a test drive.  It looks so pretty, &lt;drool&gt;.  ||||reg||1
